<section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap"><div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">01 / Choose a first shortlist</p><h2>Which CRM fits<br>your small business?</h2><p>Pick two to trial. Import a small sample of real enquiries and see whether the team can find the next action without help.</p></div><div class="sg-table-wrap"><table class="lp-table sg-table" role="table"><caption>Nine small-business CRMs: fit, named paid plan and the main drawback</caption><thead><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">CRM</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Useful for</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">Base paid plan</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">The drawback</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for p in guide.providers %}<tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader"><a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }}</a></th><td role="cell" data-label="Useful for">{{ p.fit }}</td><td role="cell" data-label="Base paid plan"><strong>${{ p.rate }} / paid user / month</strong><small>{{ p.plan }} · {{ p.billing }}</small></td><td role="cell" data-label="The drawback">{{ p.catch }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<p class="sg-note"><strong>Already running an outbound sales team?</strong> Use our <a href="/resources/best-crm-for-outbound-sales/">CRM comparison for cold calling and outbound sales</a> for diallers, sequences and campaign handoffs. Replacing HubSpot? Start with the <a href="/resources/hubspot-alternatives/">HubSpot alternatives guide</a>.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="team-cost"><div class="lp-wrap"><div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">02 / A budget you can read</p><h2>CRM costs for one,<br>three or five users.</h2><p><strong>USD base subscription per month.</strong> Annual-billing prices are monthly equivalents. HubSpot uses its standard monthly rate; Less Annoying CRM bills monthly. Taxes, phone usage, setup and separate add-ons are extra. Compare the features as well as the totals.</p></div><div class="sg-table-wrap"><table class="lp-table sg-table sg-costs" role="table"><caption>Small-business CRM base subscription totals, including the monday seat minimum</caption><thead><tr role="row"><th scope="col" role="columnheader">CRM and plan</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">1 user</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">3 users</th><th scope="col" role="columnheader">5 users</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for p in guide.providers %}<tr role="row"><th scope="row" role="rowheader"><a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }}</a><small>{{ p.plan }} · {{ p.billing }}</small></th>{% for n in [1,3,5] %}{% set seats = n %}{% if p.minimum > n %}{% set seats = p.minimum %}{% endif %}<td role="cell" data-label="{{ n }} {% if n == 1 %}user{% else %}users{% endif %}">${{ p.rate * seats }}{% if seats > n %}<small>{{ seats }} paid seats required</small>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}</tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<div class="sg-two sg-after"><div><h3>The minimum purchase changes the price.</h3><p>Three Bigin Express seats cost $21 a month equivalent, or $252 billed annually. One monday CRM Basic user still requires three seats: $36 a month equivalent, or $432 billed annually. Four monday users require five seats.</p></div><div><h3>The next tier can matter more than another user.</h3><p>Pipedrive requires Growth for full email sync. Close puts automated workflows in Growth. Price those upgrades before choosing an entry plan.</p></div></div>
