<section class="lp-section" id="crm-reviews"><div class="lp-wrap"><div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">03 / The useful strengths and limits</p><h2>Nine CRMs.<br>CallTeam's verdicts.</h2><p>Buy the features your team needs for its daily work.</p></div>{% for p in guide.providers %}<article class="lp-provider" id="{{ p.id }}"><header class="lp-provider-head"><div><p class="lp-kicker">{{ p.fit }}</p><h3>{{ p.name }}</h3></div><a class="lp-source" href="{{ p.sources[0][1] }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official pricing ↗</a></header><div class="lp-provider-body"><div class="lp-provider-detail"><h4>What works</h4><p>{{ p.good }}</p><h4>The drawback</h4><p>{{ p.weak }}</p><h4>What you pay</h4><p>{{ p.extra }}</p></div><aside class="lp-verdict"><p class="lp-kicker">CallTeam's verdict</p><p class="lp-verdict-text">{{ p.verdict }}</p></aside></div><p class="lp-sources">Official sources: {% for s in p.sources %}<a href="{{ s[1] }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ s[0] }} ↗</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p></article>{% endfor %}</div></section>

<section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="free-crm"><div class="lp-wrap"><div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">04 / Start without a subscription</p><h2>Which free CRM<br>is actually usable?</h2><p>Check the user, record and feature limits before importing your list.</p></div><div class="sg-two"><div><h3>HubSpot, Zoho and Freshsales</h3><p><strong>HubSpot Free:</strong> up to two users and 1,000 contacts. It is worth testing for a very small team handling enquiries and sales.</p><p><strong>Zoho CRM Free and Freshsales Free:</strong> up to three users. Check their free-edition features against the paid plans above; the allowances are different.</p></div><div><h3>Bigin, trials and paid seats</h3><p><strong>Bigin Free:</strong> one user and 500 records. Activities and notes count towards the allowance, so a busy owner can reach it quickly.</p><p>Pipedrive, monday CRM and Less Annoying CRM offer time-limited trials. Budget for the subscription after the trial ends.</p></div></div><p class="sg-note"><strong>Our advice:</strong> stay on the free plan until a limit blocks your work. Pay for the feature or seat you need.</p></div></section>

<section class="lp-section" id="first-crm-decisions"><div class="lp-wrap"><div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">05 / Make the purchase useful</p><h2>What your first CRM<br>needs to do.</h2></div><div class="sg-flow"><div><h3>Keep one customer record.</h3><p>Import a small sample with company, contact, owner, deal stage and next action. Remove duplicates before the full import. Keep shared inbox history and personal notes attached to the right person.</p></div><div><h3>Show the overdue work.</h3><p>Ask the actual user to find today's callbacks and overdue enquiries. If the task needs a manager to explain three screens every morning, simplify the setup.</p></div><div><h3>Let you take the data out.</h3><p>Export the sample before importing everything. Check which notes, activities and tasks come with it. A contact CSV alone may leave out the history you need.</p><p>For leads from automated LinkedIn campaigns, check who receives the reply and records the next action. Our <a href="/resources/best-linkedin-automation-tools/">LinkedIn outreach tool comparison</a> covers those workflow limits and sender costs.</p></div></div>
<div class="sg-two sg-after"><div><h3>HubSpot vs Pipedrive for a first CRM</h3><p>Choose HubSpot when forms, enquiries and the wider marketing setup need a shared record. Choose Pipedrive when the immediate problem is seeing live deals and their next activities. Test the required email features on the plan you intend to buy.</p></div><div><h3>Bigin vs Zoho CRM for a small team</h3><p>Choose Bigin for a straightforward sales pipeline. Choose Zoho CRM when you need more control over ownership, reporting or automation.</p></div></div>
<div class="sg-note"><strong>Where does Apollo fit?</strong> Apollo combines prospect data with outreach and deal features. Test it against your ownership, history and follow-up needs before treating it as the main CRM. For buying contact data, use our <a href="/resources/b2b-lead-providers/">lead generation database comparison</a>; for replacing it, use <a href="/resources/apollo-alternatives/">Apollo alternatives for cold calling</a>.</div>
</div></section>

